# AGENTS.md

Instructions for AI coding agents working on this BranchKit plugin
(`{{.PluginID}}`, Python). People should start with `README.md`.

BranchKit is a desktop plugin platform. A plugin is a separate process that
speaks JSON-RPC with the BranchKit app. Its manifest, `plugin.json`, declares
everything it provides and everything it needs.

## The loop

```bash
branchkit-cli dev test .       # checks the plugin, runs it under the test harness
python3 -m unittest            # this plugin's own tests, under the test harness
```

You are done when `branchkit-cli dev test .` and the plugin's own tests pass.
Neither touches the running app. Install into the app only when the user asks
(`branchkit-cli plugin install .`): the app on their machine is in use.

## Read the docs before guessing an API

The platform docs ship with the app as markdown, matching the installed
version:

```bash
D="$(branchkit-cli docs path)"
cat "$D/llms.txt"                  # one line per page
grep -rn "<term>" "$D"
```

